		{"m3-long-laptop", "my laptop finally died today. it had been making a weird clicking noise for weeks and this morning it just would not turn on, black screen, nothing. i took it to the repair place near the train station and the guy said the logic board is fried and it would cost almost as much to fix as a new one. so now i am laptop shopping, which i hate, because every review site says something different and every model has some weird tradeoff. i think i am going to get the same brand again because i know how it works, just a newer version with more memory. luckily almost everything was backed up to the cloud except a folder of photos from last summer that i forgot to sync, which i am sad about. the repair guy said he might be able to pull the drive and recover them for like sixty dollars so i left it with him. in the meantime i am using my old tablet with a keyboard case, which is fine for email but terrible for anything real. work is lending me a loaner for the week, so at least i can do my job. lesson learned, sync everything, always, immediately. i also need to remember to wipe the old one before i recycle it, there is a lot of personal stuff on there.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"m3-long-wedding", "my best friend from college, aisha, is getting married in june and asked me to be a bridesmaid, which i am thrilled about and also a little terrified because there are like nine bridesmaids and a group chat that never sleeps. the wedding is in savannah, which i have never been to, and everyone says it is beautiful in early summer if a little humid. the dresses are sage green and we each get to pick our own style, which is nice because i look terrible in strapless. there is a bachelorette weekend in april that might be in nashville, the group chat has been arguing about it for days. i need to book flights soon because prices are already going up, and figure out where to stay since the hotel block is pretty expensive. i might split an airbnb with two of the other bridesmaids. i also have to give a toast at the rehearsal dinner, aisha asked me specifically, so i need to start writing it now instead of the night before like i would normally do. i have so many embarrassing stories from college, the trick will be picking ones that are funny but will not get me uninvited.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"m3-long-neighbor", "neighbor drama update, because apparently i live in a soap opera now. the guy downstairs has been complaining that my footsteps are too loud, which, i walk like a normal person, but fine, i bought rugs. then last week he left a note on my door about my bike in the hallway, even though there is literally no other place to put it, the bike room has been full for months. the building manager said she would talk to him and also that a bike spot might finally open up in february. meanwhile the couple across the hall are the nicest people alive, they brought me soup when i was sick and they water my plants when i travel. their daughter is selling girl scout cookies so obviously i ordered six boxes, mostly thin mints, which i am not proud of. i am trying to stay neutral and polite with the downstairs guy because i still have to live here for another month before the move. at least the new building has a proper bike room and nobody below us on the ground floor, just the laundry room, so i can walk as loudly as i want.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"m3-long-class", "i signed up for a pottery class on wednesday nights and it is the most humbling thing i have ever done. the instructor makes it look so easy, she just touches the clay and it turns into a perfect bowl, and then i touch it and it collapses into a sad lump. after three weeks i have made exactly one thing that holds water, a lopsided little cup that i love unreasonably. there are eight people in the class, a retired teacher who is weirdly amazing at it, a couple on a date night, two college students, and a guy who only makes ashtrays. the studio is in an old warehouse near the river and smells like wet earth in a good way. the class costs 180 for eight weeks plus 20 for clay, which feels like a lot but it is the only two hours a week where i do not look at my phone. the final class is in mid january and we get to glaze and fire everything we made. i am planning to give the cup to my mom, she will pretend it is beautiful, which is what moms are for.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"m3-long-budget", "money check in because the move is making me nervous about spending. i went through my bank statements for the last three months and i spend way more on food delivery than i thought, like three hundred a month, which is wild. i set a goal to cut that in half by cooking more and packing lunch. the moving costs are adding up too, the movers, the deposit, new furniture, a few hundred for random stuff like shower curtains and hangers. i made a separate savings account just for the move and put fifteen hundred in it, which should cover most of it if i am careful. i also finally opened a retirement account at work, i had been putting it off for two years because the forms were confusing, but hr walked me through it and now four percent goes in every paycheck with a match. it felt like a very adult moment. my next goal is building an emergency fund of three months of expenses, which feels far away but doable if i stop ordering pad thai at midnight. small steps.", "text", ""}, ¬
