		{"n-file-cover", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/file-cover-letter.docx||sent it", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"n-ramble-1", "ok so today was weird i woke up late bc my alarm didnt go off and then the train was packed and some guy spilled coffee on my shoes which like ok cool great start. work was meetings meetings meetings, lena wants the onboarding thing demo ready by next friday which is insane but whatever we'll make it work i think. lunch was the sad salad again i rly need to start bringing food. dana texted about climbing tmrw i said yes even tho my arms still hurt from last time lol. then after work i went to target for hangers and came out with like 80 dollars of stuff i didnt need including a lamp shaped like a mushroom which jess is gonna hate or love idk. also my mom called and asked if i was eating vegetables and i lied. then i watched like 3 episodes of the baking show and fell asleep on the couch again. need to fix my sleep schedule fr. oh and the laptop guy called he got the photos off the old drive so thats one good thing today", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"n-ramble-2", "random thoughts bc i cant sleep. thinking abt whether to adopt waffles before or after the move, prob after bc moving w a dog sounds like chaos. jess says after too. also i rly want to go to portugal in the spring but money is tight w the move so maybe fall instead?? idk. aisha's wedding is in june so thats another trip. i also need to call grandma back she left me a voicemail thats just her saying call me back 3 times in a row lmao. work stuff is fine, the reorg was weird but lena seems good. i think im gonna try to wake up at 630 and walk before work starting monday. famous last words. also the guy downstairs left ANOTHER note about my bike. its literally the only place it fits. 4 more weeks in this building. 4 more weeks.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"n-ramble-3", "ok weekend recap bc i promised myself id write stuff down more. sat morning farmers market w sofia, got the honeycrisp apples and a weird purple cauliflower that tasted normal. then we got coffee at the place on 4th and they had cardamom buns which were incredible. afternoon i packed like 3 boxes which is progress. sat night jess came over and we planned furniture, we measured the living room again its 11ft 4 and the green couch def wont fit w the bookshelf so maybe a smaller couch or no bookshelf. sunday i did nothing except laundry and made the tahini sauce thing for the grain bowls, it worked!! ate it 3 times. then i video called aisha abt bridesmaid stuff for an hour, the bachelorette might be nashville or new orleans, group chat is split. i voted nashville.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"n-ramble-4", "work rant incoming. so the client wants the dashboard redesign by feb AND they want to add 3 new features AND they dont want to pay more. my manager said she'll push back but idk how hard. then in standup someone said the onboarding demo was 'basically done' which is a lie, its like 60 percent done max. i have 2 interviews to run next week for the new engineer role, i have literally never interviewed anyone before so lena is gonna sit in on the first one. also the coffee machine broke AGAIN. and our team slack channel is just people sending memes about the coffee machine. ok actually that part is funny. leaving early tmrw for the dentist, cleaning at 3, havent been in over a year so its gonna be a whole thing", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"n-ramble-5", "late night brain dump. stuff i need to do before the move: book the movers for real (bluebird, jan 2), get renters insurance, set up internet at the new place, forward my mail, cancel the gym near my old place and sign up for the one by the park, return the library books, give the plants to the neighbors across the hall for a week, pack the kitchen last, label every box this time bc last time i opened 9 boxes looking for one fork. also i should prob deep clean so i get my deposit back, the oven is a crime scene. jess is handling the wifi and the couch stuff. i'm handling movers and insurance. we made a shared list. its very organized. im proud of us", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"n-ramble-6", "ok last one i promise. went to pottery and finally made a bowl that doesnt leak, the instructor said it was my best one yet and i almost cried which is embarrassing over a bowl. then got ramen w dana after, she's leaving the team which sucks but we'll still climb on tuesdays. she told me about this book on salt which apparently is the next book club pick, sounds boring but mira insists. then came home and my neighbor's kid was selling girl scout cookies so obv i bought 6 boxes of thin mints. thats my whole personality now. thin mints and pottery. goodnight", "text", ""}, ¬
