		{"z-p-reset", "reset", "text", "Satchel"}, ¬
		{"z-p-hi", "hey", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-p-conference", "ok so the conference week was a lot and i want to write it all down before i forget. i flew into denver on monday morning and the airport was chaos, there was some kind of ground stop because of snow in chicago so half the gates were packed with people sleeping on the floor. the shuttle to the hotel took forever and the driver kept missing turns, which honestly was kind of funny after a while. the hotel was one of those huge convention center ones with a fake waterfall in the lobby and about nine restaurants that all serve the same burger. check in was slow but they gave me a room on a high floor with a view of the mountains, it was room 1408 which made me think of that stephen king movie and i did not sleep great the first night because of it. the first day of the conference was mostly registration and a welcome reception where i met a bunch of people from other companies doing similar work. there was a guy from a logistics startup who would not stop talking about route optimization and a woman named priyanka from a hospital system who was actually super interesting, she is building a scheduling tool for nurses and has the same problems we have with shift changes. tuesday was the big day. the keynote was given by dr. amara okafor, who runs a research lab on human attention and interfaces, and it was genuinely the best talk i have seen in years. she talked about how people only remember things they act on within the first day and how most tools ignore that, which made me think about basically every product i have ever worked on. after that there were breakout sessions and i went to one on accessibility, one on design systems, and one on onboarding that was mostly a sales pitch disguised as a talk. lunch was a sad boxed sandwich again. in the afternoon our team had a booth and i stood there for four hours explaining our product to people, my feet still hurt. wednesday i skipped the morning sessions because i was exhausted and walked around downtown, there is a great used bookstore near the convention center with like three floors and a cat that sleeps on the poetry shelf. i bought two books i will never read. in the afternoon i went to a workshop on research interviews which was actually useful, they had us practice asking open questions instead of leading ones and i was way worse at it than i thought. wednesday night a few of us went to a brewery and then a karaoke bar and i will not be discussing what i sang. thursday was the last full day and mostly panels, one of which got heated when two people disagreed about whether ai features should be opt in or opt out. i think both of them were kind of right. i had dinner with my manager and we talked about next year and she hinted that i might get to lead the new onboarding project, which would be huge. friday is the travel day, my flight home is ua 2231 at 6:15 pm so i have most of the day to pack and maybe see the art museum. i am also supposed to bring back something for the team, probably chocolates from that fancy place in the lobby. overall it was exhausting but really good, i have pages of notes and a bunch of new contacts and i feel more motivated about work than i have in months.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-n-shot-parking", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/shot-parking.png||here", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-n-cryptic-1", "claude sub 100", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-p-apartment", "apartment hunting update because i finally found a place and i signed the lease yesterday. it took like six weeks of looking and i saw maybe fifteen apartments, most of which were either way too expensive, way too small, or had something weird like a bathroom with no door or a kitchen in the hallway. the one i got is a two bedroom on the third floor of an older building near the park, with big windows and real wood floors and a radiator that clanks a lot but works. my roommate is going to be jess, my friend from college who just moved back to the city, so we are splitting it. the landlord is an older guy named mr. patel who owns three buildings on the block and seems very nice, he gave us a whole tour and told us the history of the building, apparently it used to be a hat factory. rent is 2,350 a month total so it comes out to 1,175 each which is a little more than i wanted but way better than the other places we saw. the lease starts january 3 and runs for a year. we need to get renters insurance before move in and set up internet, mr. patel said most people in the building use the fiber company. there is a laundry room in the basement which is a huge upgrade from my current place where i have to go to the laundromat. the only downside is no dishwasher, so we will see how long jess and i stay friends. i also need to figure out movers, my friend recommended a company that is cheap but apparently they broke her mirror so maybe not them. i am going to start packing slowly over the holidays so i am not doing it all at the last minute like last time.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-r-dinner", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/real/02-indian-dinner-naan-curry.jpg||dinner last night 🤤", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-n-link-pomodoro", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pomodoro_Technique", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-p-health", "health stuff this month, mostly good news. my knee has been bugging me since the summer so i finally started physical therapy two weeks ago. my physical therapist is a guy named kenji who is very calm and very strict, he said to do the resistance band exercises three times a week and to stop running for at least a month, which i am not happy about but whatever. he also said my hips are weak which is apparently why my knee hurts, so most of the exercises are actually for my hips. i also did my yearly physical and got blood work done. most of it was fine, cholesterol normal, blood sugar normal, but my vitamin d was 18 which the doctor said is pretty low, so i have to take a supplement every day and get rechecked in three months. she also said to get more sun which is hard in winter. i booked a dentist cleaning for next month too since i have not been in over a year, which is embarrassing. trying to actually take care of myself this year instead of waiting until something hurts.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-r-scoreboard", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/real/03-sixers-arena-scoreboard.jpg", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-n-memo-vet", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/memo-vet.m4a", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-p-cat", "so i am cat sitting for my neighbor while she is away for the holidays, her cat is named mochi and she is a very fluffy gray cat who hates everyone except my neighbor. the door code for her apartment is 7731 and the cat food is in the cabinet above the fridge. mochi eats at 7am and 6pm, half a can each time plus a scoop of dry food, and she has to take a pill crushed into the morning food. the litter box is in the bathroom and needs to be cleaned every other day. my neighbor said mochi will probably hide under the bed for the first two days and that is normal. she gets back on the 30th.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-r-arch", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/real/06-drexel-building-arch.jpg||walked by this", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-n-cryptic-3", "gym lockr 4482", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-p2-long-sports", "random rant but i have been watching way too much basketball lately and i think my team is cursed. every single season we start strong and then someone important gets hurt in january and we limp into the playoffs as a seven seed and lose in the first round. this year it was our point guard, he rolled his ankle stepping on someone's foot, which is the most basketball injury possible. my dad keeps texting me trade ideas that would never happen, like trading three bench guys for an all star, and i keep telling him that is not how the salary cap works but he does not care. we watched the game last night at the bar near my office and the place was packed, the bartender knew everyone by name except me. i had wings that were way too spicy and i regretted it for hours. also the refs were terrible, i know everyone says that but they really were. anyway the season is long and there is still time for them to break my heart in new and creative ways. on a totally different note, jess's wifi is hatfactory22 btw, she set it up early so we can test it when we visit the new place this weekend. also i finally fixed my bike, it needed a new chain and the shop guy said the brakes were basically held together by hope, so i got those replaced too and now it feels like a new bike. i rode it to the park on saturday and it was freezing but the lake was frozen and really pretty, there were people ice skating near the edge which seemed insane to me.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-r-video", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/real/09-video.mov||!!!", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-n-file-warranty", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/file-warranty.pdf", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-p2-long-show", "ok i need to talk about this show. i started watching the one about the lighthouse keeper on the island where everyone has secrets and i finished all eight episodes in two days which is not something i am proud of. the main character is this quiet guy who moved there after his wife died and it slowly turns out that the whole town knew her before he did, which is creepy and also kind of sad. there is a twist in episode six that i did not see coming at all, i actually yelled at my tv. jess says the book is better but she says that about everything. the music is incredible too, all cello and wind sounds. i want to go to a place like that someday, somewhere foggy and remote with no wifi. which reminds me, the movers quoted 840 for jan 2, the ones with good reviews, not the mirror breakers, so i think we are going with them, they are called bluebird moving. i need to confirm by friday or they give the date away. also my coworker brought in homemade dumplings today and they were so good i asked for the recipe, she said it is her grandmother's and she will only share it if i promise to make them for the team potluck, which, deal. work otherwise was boring, a lot of meetings about meetings. the onboarding project kickoff got moved to next tuesday, my manager wants me to present the research plan which is exciting and terrifying.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-r-mascot", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/real/08-sixers-court-mascot.jpg", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-n-video-tour", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/video-tour.mp4||for jess", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-r-avatar", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/real/01-avatar-cartoon.png", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-n-cryptic-4", "cafe wifi beanthere22", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-p2-long-weather", "weather here is so weird lately, it was sixty degrees on monday and then snowing on wednesday, my body does not know what season it is. i have three different jackets by the door now. i went to the farmers market on sunday anyway and they had the best apples, those honeycrisp ones that cost like four dollars each but are worth it. there was a guy selling hot cider and another guy playing banjo very badly but enthusiastically. my usual order at the coffee place by work is an oat cortado and they finally started remembering it, which made me feel like a real regular. i also tried the new bakery on 4th, the cardamom buns are amazing and they sell out by 10 so you have to go early. otherwise i have been trying to read more, i am halfway through a book about the history of maps and it is surprisingly fun, there is a whole chapter about made up islands that stayed on maps for centuries because nobody bothered to check. my mom called and wants everyone home for christmas eve dinner at 5, she is making the lasagna again and i am supposed to bring dessert, i am thinking of trying those cardamom buns or just buying a pie and pretending i made it. my brother is bringing his new girlfriend, her name is talia and apparently she is a vet, so mochi questions will finally have an expert.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-r-pastry", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/real/05-cafe-pastry-purple-hoodie.jpg", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-n-link-yosemite", "https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/camping.htm||camping maybe", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-r-posters", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/real/07-penn-engineering-posters.jpg", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-m2-memo", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/memo-plumber.m4a", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-r-player", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/real/04-sixers-player-23-closeup.jpg||lol", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-m2-itinerary", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/itinerary.docx", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-m2-video-hike", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/video-hike.mp4", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-n-cryptic-2", "car reg due 3/15 dont forget", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-p6-shot-receipt", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/shot-receipt.png||movers receipt", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-p6-shot-sparse", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/shot-sparse.png", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-n-shot-ticket", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/shot-ticket.png||!!!!", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-n-file-cover", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/file-cover-letter.docx||sent it", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-m2-packing", "file:~/Pictures/satchel-test/packing-list.txt", "tapback", ""}, ¬
		{"z-n-cryptic-5", "mom bday scarf?? or the frame", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-p2-long-plans", "trying to plan the new year stuff already because otherwise it never happens. jess and i want to do a small housewarming in mid january once we are moved in, just a few friends, maybe twelve people max because the apartment is not that big. i want to make a big pot of chili and have people bring drinks. the date we picked is january 17 which is a saturday. i also want to finally get a real couch instead of the one from college that has a mystery stain, there is a furniture store near the new place having a sale and the green velvet one i liked is 899 down from 1,200, i might just do it. for work my goal next year is to actually ship the onboarding project and not let it drag for eighteen months like the last one. personally i want to run a half marathon in the spring if kenji ever lets me run again, and read twenty books, and call my grandparents more. i also want to learn to make bread properly, there is a class at the community center on thursday nights that starts in february and costs 120 for six weeks. that feels doable. and i want to take a real trip somewhere, maybe portugal or japan, somewhere i have never been, but that depends on money after the move.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-p6-long-1", "today was one of those days where nothing went wrong exactly but everything took twice as long. the train was delayed twenty minutes because of a signal problem so i got to work late and missed the first half of standup, then the coffee machine on our floor broke so i had to go downstairs to the cafe where the line was out the door. i finally sat down at like 10 and had forty unread messages, half of which were people asking the same question in different channels. we are migrating to a new ticket system and nobody knows where anything is anymore, my team lead keeps saying it will be worth it in the long run which is what people always say about painful things. lunch was a salad that was mostly croutons. in the afternoon i had a one on one with my skip level manager which went fine, she asked about my career goals and i panicked and said something vague about growth. i should actually think about that before the next one. after work i went to the grocery store and forgot the one thing i went there for, which was laundry detergent, and came home with snacks instead. dinner was frozen dumplings and a whole episode of a cooking competition show where someone cried over a soufflé. i related to them deeply.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-p6-long-2", "my sister came over this weekend with her kids and it was chaos in the best way. the twins are four now and they have discovered that if they scream at the exact same time it makes a sound that can probably be heard from space. we built a blanket fort in the living room that took up the entire floor and they made me crawl through it like a tunnel about thirty times. then we made pancakes shaped like dinosaurs, which were really just blobs with a tail, and they loved them anyway. my sister and i finally got to talk for like twenty minutes while they watched a movie, she is thinking about going back to school for nursing which i think is amazing, she has always been the person everyone calls when they are sick. she is worried about the cost and the time with two kids but her husband is supportive. we also talked about our parents' anniversary and she still wants the cabin, i still want the dinner, we agreed to do both again because we are incapable of choosing. after they left my apartment looked like a tornado went through it and i found a toy car in my shoe the next morning.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-p6-long-3", "thinking about getting a dog again. i have wanted one for years but my old apartment did not allow pets and now the new place does, mr patel said dogs under fifty pounds are fine with a pet deposit. jess is on board as long as it is not a puppy that chews everything, so i am looking at adult rescues. there is a shelter across town that does adoption days on saturdays and they have a three year old beagle mix named waffles who looks very chill in his photos. i also like the idea of a greyhound because apparently they are huge couch potatoes despite being fast. i need to figure out the budget, food and vet and insurance and a walker on days i go into the office, it adds up to maybe two hundred a month. my coworker has a dog walker she loves who charges twenty five per walk. i keep looking at dog beds online like i already have a dog. the plan is to wait until after we move in and settle for a few weeks, then go to an adoption day in february. i am trying not to get too attached to waffles in case he gets adopted before then, but i already kind of am.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-p6-long-4", "ok random but i have been trying to cook more and this week was a disaster and a success at the same time. monday i tried to make risotto and stirred it for forty minutes and it came out like glue, i think i used the wrong rice. tuesday i gave up and ordered thai food. wednesday i made a sheet pan dinner with chicken thighs, potatoes, and broccoli, which was so easy and so good that i made it again thursday. friday i tried baking bread from a no knead recipe and it actually worked, crispy crust and everything, i sent a picture to my mom and she called me immediately to say she was proud, which was a little much but also nice. the trick is apparently a dutch oven, which i borrowed from jess. saturday i made chili again for my neighbor who just had surgery, she was very grateful and gave me a jar of homemade jam in return. sunday i meal prepped lunches for the week, mostly grain bowls with roasted vegetables and a tahini sauce i found on the internet. i spent way less on takeout this week, maybe forty dollars instead of the usual hundred and fifty, so i am counting that as a win.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-p6-long-5", "work drama update. the reorg finally happened and our team got split in half, some people are moving to the platform team and some are staying on product. i am staying, which i am glad about, but two of my favorite coworkers are leaving the team, including dana, which is a bummer because she was the person i ate lunch with every day. we are still going to climb on tuesdays though. my new team lead is someone from the design side, named lena, who seems smart and very organized, she sent a doc with team norms on her first day which honestly i appreciate. the onboarding project is officially mine to lead now, which is exciting and terrifying, the kickoff went well and people seemed into the research plan. we have to ship a first version by the end of march. i also have to hire one more engineer for the team, which means a lot of interviews in january. i have never been on the hiring side much so i am a little nervous about doing it well. lena said she would pair with me on the first few. overall it feels like a fresh start, even if i miss the old group.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-p6-long-6", "random thoughts before bed. i really need to call my grandparents, it has been like three weeks and they always act like it has been three years. i also want to start journaling again, i used to do it every night in college and it helped me sleep. i found my old journal when packing and it was so embarrassing, so many pages about a guy whose name i do not even remember. i want to plan a trip for the spring, maybe portugal, jess says lisbon is amazing and cheap, or maybe japan if i can save enough. i should start a savings account just for travel. also my car needs an oil change and i have been ignoring the little light for two weeks, which is probably bad. and i promised to help my friend move a couch on saturday, which is ironic since i am about to move myself. i think i am going to try to wake up earlier next week, like 6:30, and go for a walk before work. we will see how long that lasts. goodnight to no one.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-p6-long-7", "book club was last night and it was so much fun, way better than i expected. mira hosted again and made this incredible spinach dip and a cheese board that looked like a magazine photo. we discussed the generation ship book and the ending split the group in half, some people loved that it was ambiguous and some people, including dana, were furious that it did not explain anything. i was somewhere in the middle, i liked the mystery but i wanted one more chapter. the nurse in the group had a whole theory about the captain being an ai the whole time which honestly made more sense than the actual book. we picked the next book, it is a nonfiction one about the history of salt which sounds boring but mira swears it is fascinating. after the discussion we just hung out and talked about everything else for two hours, jobs and dating and someone's terrible landlord. i walked home with the teacher from the group, her name is sofia, and it turns out she lives three blocks from my new apartment so we might start walking to the farmers market together on sundays. i love having a regular thing on the calendar that is not work.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-p6-long-8", "ok holiday shopping panic has officially started. i made a list on my phone and it is long. for my mom i am getting the digital photo frame and loading it with pictures of the twins and theo, my sister is splitting it with me. for my dad a fancy coffee grinder because his broke and he keeps complaining about it. for my brother and talia a board game they mentioned, the one with the trains. for jess i want to get something for the new apartment, maybe a nice plant or a cool lamp. for dana a climbing chalk bag with a funny design. for my grandparents a framed family photo. for the twins those dinosaur pajamas that light up, they will lose their minds. i still need to figure out something for my neighbor as a thank you for the jam. budget is about five hundred total which is already stretched. i am going to try to do most of it online this week so i do not have to go to the mall, the mall in december is my personal nightmare. also need wrapping paper, tape, and to remember where i put the gift bags from last year, probably in a box i already packed for the move.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-m3-long-laptop", "my laptop finally died today. it had been making a weird clicking noise for weeks and this morning it just would not turn on, black screen, nothing. i took it to the repair place near the train station and the guy said the logic board is fried and it would cost almost as much to fix as a new one. so now i am laptop shopping, which i hate, because every review site says something different and every model has some weird tradeoff. i think i am going to get the same brand again because i know how it works, just a newer version with more memory. luckily almost everything was backed up to the cloud except a folder of photos from last summer that i forgot to sync, which i am sad about. the repair guy said he might be able to pull the drive and recover them for like sixty dollars so i left it with him. in the meantime i am using my old tablet with a keyboard case, which is fine for email but terrible for anything real. work is lending me a loaner for the week, so at least i can do my job. lesson learned, sync everything, always, immediately. i also need to remember to wipe the old one before i recycle it, there is a lot of personal stuff on there.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-m3-long-wedding", "my best friend from college, aisha, is getting married in june and asked me to be a bridesmaid, which i am thrilled about and also a little terrified because there are like nine bridesmaids and a group chat that never sleeps. the wedding is in savannah, which i have never been to, and everyone says it is beautiful in early summer if a little humid. the dresses are sage green and we each get to pick our own style, which is nice because i look terrible in strapless. there is a bachelorette weekend in april that might be in nashville, the group chat has been arguing about it for days. i need to book flights soon because prices are already going up, and figure out where to stay since the hotel block is pretty expensive. i might split an airbnb with two of the other bridesmaids. i also have to give a toast at the rehearsal dinner, aisha asked me specifically, so i need to start writing it now instead of the night before like i would normally do. i have so many embarrassing stories from college, the trick will be picking ones that are funny but will not get me uninvited.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-m3-long-neighbor", "neighbor drama update, because apparently i live in a soap opera now. the guy downstairs has been complaining that my footsteps are too loud, which, i walk like a normal person, but fine, i bought rugs. then last week he left a note on my door about my bike in the hallway, even though there is literally no other place to put it, the bike room has been full for months. the building manager said she would talk to him and also that a bike spot might finally open up in february. meanwhile the couple across the hall are the nicest people alive, they brought me soup when i was sick and they water my plants when i travel. their daughter is selling girl scout cookies so obviously i ordered six boxes, mostly thin mints, which i am not proud of. i am trying to stay neutral and polite with the downstairs guy because i still have to live here for another month before the move. at least the new building has a proper bike room and nobody below us on the ground floor, just the laundry room, so i can walk as loudly as i want.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-m3-long-class", "i signed up for a pottery class on wednesday nights and it is the most humbling thing i have ever done. the instructor makes it look so easy, she just touches the clay and it turns into a perfect bowl, and then i touch it and it collapses into a sad lump. after three weeks i have made exactly one thing that holds water, a lopsided little cup that i love unreasonably. there are eight people in the class, a retired teacher who is weirdly amazing at it, a couple on a date night, two college students, and a guy who only makes ashtrays. the studio is in an old warehouse near the river and smells like wet earth in a good way. the class costs 180 for eight weeks plus 20 for clay, which feels like a lot but it is the only two hours a week where i do not look at my phone. the final class is in mid january and we get to glaze and fire everything we made. i am planning to give the cup to my mom, she will pretend it is beautiful, which is what moms are for.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-m3-long-budget", "money check in because the move is making me nervous about spending. i went through my bank statements for the last three months and i spend way more on food delivery than i thought, like three hundred a month, which is wild. i set a goal to cut that in half by cooking more and packing lunch. the moving costs are adding up too, the movers, the deposit, new furniture, a few hundred for random stuff like shower curtains and hangers. i made a separate savings account just for the move and put fifteen hundred in it, which should cover most of it if i am careful. i also finally opened a retirement account at work, i had been putting it off for two years because the forms were confusing, but hr walked me through it and now four percent goes in every paycheck with a match. it felt like a very adult moment. my next goal is building an emergency fund of three months of expenses, which feels far away but doable if i stop ordering pad thai at midnight. small steps.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-n-ramble-1", "ok so today was weird i woke up late bc my alarm didnt go off and then the train was packed and some guy spilled coffee on my shoes which like ok cool great start. work was meetings meetings meetings, lena wants the onboarding thing demo ready by next friday which is insane but whatever we'll make it work i think. lunch was the sad salad again i rly need to start bringing food. dana texted about climbing tmrw i said yes even tho my arms still hurt from last time lol. then after work i went to target for hangers and came out with like 80 dollars of stuff i didnt need including a lamp shaped like a mushroom which jess is gonna hate or love idk. also my mom called and asked if i was eating vegetables and i lied. then i watched like 3 episodes of the baking show and fell asleep on the couch again. need to fix my sleep schedule fr. oh and the laptop guy called he got the photos off the old drive so thats one good thing today", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-n-ramble-2", "random thoughts bc i cant sleep. thinking abt whether to adopt waffles before or after the move, prob after bc moving w a dog sounds like chaos. jess says after too. also i rly want to go to portugal in the spring but money is tight w the move so maybe fall instead?? idk. aisha's wedding is in june so thats another trip. i also need to call grandma back she left me a voicemail thats just her saying call me back 3 times in a row lmao. work stuff is fine, the reorg was weird but lena seems good. i think im gonna try to wake up at 630 and walk before work starting monday. famous last words. also the guy downstairs left ANOTHER note about my bike. its literally the only place it fits. 4 more weeks in this building. 4 more weeks.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-n-ramble-3", "ok weekend recap bc i promised myself id write stuff down more. sat morning farmers market w sofia, got the honeycrisp apples and a weird purple cauliflower that tasted normal. then we got coffee at the place on 4th and they had cardamom buns which were incredible. afternoon i packed like 3 boxes which is progress. sat night jess came over and we planned furniture, we measured the living room again its 11ft 4 and the green couch def wont fit w the bookshelf so maybe a smaller couch or no bookshelf. sunday i did nothing except laundry and made the tahini sauce thing for the grain bowls, it worked!! ate it 3 times. then i video called aisha abt bridesmaid stuff for an hour, the bachelorette might be nashville or new orleans, group chat is split. i voted nashville.", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-n-ramble-4", "work rant incoming. so the client wants the dashboard redesign by feb AND they want to add 3 new features AND they dont want to pay more. my manager said she'll push back but idk how hard. then in standup someone said the onboarding demo was 'basically done' which is a lie, its like 60 percent done max. i have 2 interviews to run next week for the new engineer role, i have literally never interviewed anyone before so lena is gonna sit in on the first one. also the coffee machine broke AGAIN. and our team slack channel is just people sending memes about the coffee machine. ok actually that part is funny. leaving early tmrw for the dentist, cleaning at 3, havent been in over a year so its gonna be a whole thing", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-n-ramble-5", "late night brain dump. stuff i need to do before the move: book the movers for real (bluebird, jan 2), get renters insurance, set up internet at the new place, forward my mail, cancel the gym near my old place and sign up for the one by the park, return the library books, give the plants to the neighbors across the hall for a week, pack the kitchen last, label every box this time bc last time i opened 9 boxes looking for one fork. also i should prob deep clean so i get my deposit back, the oven is a crime scene. jess is handling the wifi and the couch stuff. i'm handling movers and insurance. we made a shared list. its very organized. im proud of us", "text", ""}, ¬
		{"z-n-ramble-6", "ok last one i promise. went to pottery and finally made a bowl that doesnt leak, the instructor said it was my best one yet and i almost cried which is embarrassing over a bowl. then got ramen w dana after, she's leaving the team which sucks but we'll still climb on tuesdays. she told me about this book on salt which apparently is the next book club pick, sounds boring but mira insists. then came home and my neighbor's kid was selling girl scout cookies so obv i bought 6 boxes of thin mints. thats my whole personality now. thin mints and pottery. goodnight", "text", ""}, ¬
